# Legends of the Twins — River of Time spells, pp.24-27 (the 'Boatsman's Guide' spellbook), and Tear of Veil's Parting, p.156. Book note (p.27): the DM is advised to keep these spells out of the free spells gained on a new level and out of easy reach of divine casters; known only by rumor, research or quest.
Confluence	TYPE:Arcane	SCHOOL:Divination	CLASSES:Sorcerer=2|Wizard=2	COMPS:V, S, M	CASTTIME:1 standard action	RANGE:See text	TARGETAREA:One person or object	DURATION:Instant	SAVEINFO:None	SPELLRES:No	DESC:Call to mind a person or object you have seen and can picture, and learn whether it has ever been at your current location and, if so, when it was last there (a brief flash, nothing more). Your location is a radius of 3 ft./level, or the room you are in if indoors or aboard ship; the spell does not move with you. Material component: a pinch of fine sand.	SOURCEPAGE:p.24
Frozen Moment	TYPE:Arcane	SCHOOL:Evocation	CLASSES:Sorcerer=4|Wizard=4	COMPS:V, S, M	CASTTIME:1 standard action	RANGE:Close (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels)	TARGETAREA:One creature or object	DURATION:1 round/level	SAVEINFO:Will	SPELLRES:Yes	DESC:Time stops flowing around the target, immobilizing it; while the spell lasts it is invulnerable to attacks, spells and damage of any kind. Affects nothing larger than Medium. Material component: a drop of water.	SOURCEPAGE:p.24
Historic Vision	TYPE:Arcane.Divine	SCHOOL:Divination	CLASSES:Cleric=2|Mystic=2|Sorcerer=1|Wizard=1	COMPS:V	CASTTIME:1 standard action	RANGE:Touch	TARGETAREA:One object or creature	DURATION:Instant	SAVEINFO:None	SPELLRES:Yes (harmless)	DESC:Learn how old the object or creature is and how long it has been in its current immediate location. On a refurbished item it shows the original age and the age since restoration, if most of the original remains (otherwise only the time since refurbishment). Works only on living creatures, or objects or mechanisms of Colossal size or smaller.	SOURCEPAGE:p.24-25
Past-Seeing	TYPE:Arcane.Divine	SCHOOL:Divination	CLASSES:Cleric=5|Mystic=5|Druid=4|Sorcerer=4|Wizard=4	COMPS:V, S, F	CASTTIME:1 minute	RANGE:Touch	TARGETAREA:One object or creature	DURATION:1 min./level	SAVEINFO:Will negates	SPELLRES:Yes (harmless)	DESC:See and hear into the target's past, up to one week per caster level back, at a moment you name (it may be as vague as "when this dagger killed the Lord Mayor"). You perceive the target and about a 10-ft. radius around it, sight and sound only, for up to 1 minute per level. Focus: a small disk of crystal or glass.	SOURCEPAGE:p.25
River's Ravages	TYPE:Arcane.Divine	SCHOOL:Transmutation	CLASSES:Druid=2|Sorcerer=2|Wizard=2	COMPS:V, S, M	CASTTIME:1 standard action	RANGE:Short (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels)	TARGETAREA:One creature	DURATION:1 round/level	SAVEINFO:Fortitude negates	SPELLRES:Yes	DESC:Age or un-age the target's body by up to 2 years per caster level, your choice of direction and amount. Memories, XP, class levels and Int, Wis and Cha are unchanged, but the physical effects of aging (PHB Chapter 6) apply, so Str, Dex and Con may change. A change of age category gives +5 circumstance on Bluff and Disguise checks to conceal identity. Cannot make the target younger than adulthood or older than its maximum age, and deals no damage. Material component: a seed and a dried leaf from the same kind of plant.	SOURCEPAGE:p.25
River's Ravages (Greater)	TYPE:Arcane.Divine	SCHOOL:Transmutation	CLASSES:Druid=7|Sorcerer=8|Wizard=8	COMPS:V, S, M, XP	CASTTIME:1 standard action	RANGE:Short (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels)	TARGETAREA:One creature	DURATION:Permanent	SAVEINFO:Fortitude negates	SPELLRES:Yes	DESC:As river's ravages, but permanent; only a wish or miracle cast by a higher-level caster removes it. Material component: a seed and a dried leaf from the same kind of plant. XP cost: 100 XP per year aged, or 500 XP per year made younger.	SOURCEPAGE:p.25
River's Ravaging Flood	TYPE:Arcane.Divine	SCHOOL:Transmutation	CLASSES:Druid=4|Sorcerer=5|Wizard=5	COMPS:V, S, M	CASTTIME:1 standard action	RANGE:Short (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels)	TARGETAREA:Cone-shaped burst	DURATION:1 round/level	SAVEINFO:Fortitude negates	SPELLRES:Yes	DESC:As river's ravages, but every creature in the cone is affected, all aged or made younger by the same amount. Blocked by 1 ft. of stone, water or metal, by force effects such as wall of force, and by antimagic fields. Material component: a seed and a dried leaf from the same kind of plant.	SOURCEPAGE:p.25
River Watch	TYPE:Arcane.Divine	SCHOOL:Divination	CLASSES:Cleric=6|Sorcerer=4|Wizard=4	COMPS:V, S	CASTTIME:1 standard action	RANGE:Personal	TARGETAREA:Radius of 100 ft. + 25 ft./level, centered on you	DURATION:1 min./level	SAVEINFO:None	SPELLRES:Yes (harmless)	DESC:You sense time-based spells and magic items, and anyone out of their proper time (time travelers, or those under time-based spells) glows faintly to you, brighter for stronger magic or greater displacement: reddish for the past, bluish for the future (you included, if you are a traveler). The glow shows through obstacles. The book lists V, S components but names a material component: a piece of sea glass or a wave-polished pebble.	SOURCEPAGE:p.26
Temporal Shield	TYPE:Arcane	SCHOOL:Abjuration	CLASSES:Sorcerer=2|Wizard=2	COMPS:V, S, M	CASTTIME:1 standard action	RANGE:Personal	TARGETAREA:You	DURATION:1 round/level	SAVEINFO:None	SPELLRES:Yes	DESC:A nearly invisible barrier the size and shape of a tower shield slows anything that passes through it: +6 shield bonus to AC, which also applies against incorporeal touch attacks and completely negates magic missiles fired at you. No armor check penalty or arcane spell failure. Material component: a pinch of sand.	SOURCEPAGE:p.26
Temporal Sphere	TYPE:Arcane	SCHOOL:Abjuration	CLASSES:Sorcerer=5|Wizard=5	COMPS:V, S, M	CASTTIME:1 standard action	RANGE:10 ft.	TARGETAREA:Sphere with a radius of 10 ft., centered on your position	DURATION:1 round/level	SAVEINFO:None	SPELLRES:Yes	DESC:A sphere of slowed time: you are invulnerable to attacks and spells from outside, and attacks and spells from inside cannot affect those outside. A lingering effect in the area (such as poison gas) stays inside. Those inside act only every other round. The sphere cannot be moved; crossing its edge either way is a full-round action that provokes attacks of opportunity (ethereal and incorporeal creatures too). You may dismiss it. A targeted dispel magic ends it on a caster level check (DC 10 + your caster level), as do greater dispel magic, antimagic field, disjunction and similar spells. Material component: a small glass sphere filled with sand.	SOURCEPAGE:p.26
Temporal Sphere (Mobile)	TYPE:Arcane	SCHOOL:Abjuration	CLASSES:Sorcerer=9|Wizard=9	COMPS:V, S, M	CASTTIME:1 standard action	RANGE:10 ft.	TARGETAREA:Sphere with a radius of 10 ft., centered on you	DURATION:1 round/level	SAVEINFO:None	SPELLRES:Yes	DESC:As selective temporal sphere, except that the sphere moves with you. Material component: a small golden sphere worth at least 1,000 stl, filled with an ounce of fine quartz sand worth 100 stl.	SOURCEPAGE:p.26
Temporal Sphere (Selective)	TYPE:Arcane	SCHOOL:Abjuration	CLASSES:Sorcerer=7|Wizard=7	COMPS:V, S, M	CASTTIME:1 standard action	RANGE:10 ft.	TARGETAREA:Sphere with a radius of 10 ft., centered on you	DURATION:1 round/level	SAVEINFO:None	SPELLRES:Yes	DESC:As temporal sphere, except that creatures leave it unhindered and attacks and spells from inside may affect those outside, at -2 (circumstance) for attacks made out of the sphere. Material component: a small silver sphere worth at least 500 stl, filled with sand.	SOURCEPAGE:p.26-27
Timeheal	TYPE:Arcane	SCHOOL:Transmutation	CLASSES:Sorcerer=7|Wizard=7	COMPS:V, S, M, XP	CASTTIME:1 minute	RANGE:Touch	TARGETAREA:Living creature touched	DURATION:Instantaneous	SAVEINFO:None (harmless)	SPELLRES:Yes	DESC:Send the target's body back in time to before it was wounded or ill, restoring its health then. You may send it back 1 minute per caster level safely; each minute beyond adds a cumulative 5% chance of failure. The target must have at least 1 hit point left: the spell cannot restore the dead (though it can restore a corpse to a pristine state). Material component: a small hourglass of powdered black pearls worth at least 500 stl. XP cost: 100 XP per minute reverted.	SOURCEPAGE:p.27
Time Reaver	TYPE:Arcane	SCHOOL:Transmutation	CLASSES:Sorcerer=9|Wizard=9	COMPS:V, S, M, F, XP	CASTTIME:1 hour	RANGE:Close (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels)	TARGETAREA:One-way portal through time and space	DURATION:Instantaneous	SAVEINFO:None	SPELLRES:No	DESC:A one-way portal through time and space for up to 1 traveler per 4 caster levels: up to 20 years per caster level back, or 1 year per level forward. Arriving at both the right time and place takes a Spellcraft check, DC 15 + 1 per decade back or + 1 per year forward. On a failure (50% each): the right time but 25 miles from the place per point missed in a random direction, or the right place but up to 5 years off per point missed, forward or back. Travelers cannot alter past or future, unless one is of a Chaos (Graygem) race such as kender, dwarves, minotaurs or sea elves. Officially known only to the Masters of the Towers. Material component: a magic circle of rare ingredients worth at least 10,000 stl + 1,000 stl per decade back or per year forward. Arcane focus: a major artifact, inert for 1 hour per decade back or per year forward. XP cost: 1,000 XP + 500 XP per decade back or per year forward.	SOURCEPAGE:p.27
Tear of Veil's Parting	TYPE:Arcane	SCHOOL:Transmutation	CLASSES:Wizard=7	COMPS:V, S	CASTTIME:1 standard action	RANGE:Touch	TARGETAREA:Living creature touched	DURATION:Special (see text)	SAVEINFO:None	SPELLRES:No	DESC:A tear shed on the target's head lets it pass through the Qualthan Grove to the Tower of High Sorcery at Kalaman. On entering the grove the target may make a Listen check (DC 15) to hear the grove's faint weeping, which leads to the Tower grounds; the spell ends once the target is on the grounds, and re-entering the grove needs the spell again. Known only to the Master of the Tower of Kalaman, who may teach it to favored apprentices.	SOURCEPAGE:p.156
